## Reproduction (measured, not guessed)

Ran a scratch jest spec against `/workspace/test/ut/core/utHelper` (500x400 chart, `dataZoom: [{type:'slider'}]`):

| case | `_location` | `_size` | `_shadowPolygonPts` | `group.x, group.y` |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| `xAxis:{type:'time'}`, 1 datum | `{x:75,y:348}` | `[375,30]` | `[[375,0],[0,0],[NaN,15]]` | **`NaN`**, 384.5 |
| `xAxis:{type:'time'}`, 2 data w/ same timestamp | `{x:75,y:348}` | `[375,30]` | `[[375,0],[0,0],[NaN,5.6],[NaN,24.4]]` | **`NaN`**, 384.5 |
| `yAxis:{type:'time'}` (vertical slider), 1 datum | `{x:455,y:65}` | `[255,30]` | `[[255,0],[0,0],[NaN,15]]` | **`NaN`, `NaN`** |
| `xAxis:{type:'time'}`, 3 data (control) | `{x:75,y:348}` | `[375,30]` | `[[375,0],[0,0],[0,16.9],[187.5,24.4],[375,5.6]]` | 77.8, 384.5 |
| `xAxis:{type:'category'|'value'}`, 1 datum | `{x:75,y:348}` | `[375,30]` | `[[375,0],[0,0],[**0**,15]]` | 77.8, 384.5 |

I also proved the causal chain: after rendering the broken time-axis chart I overwrote the NaN x in the polygon/polyline shapes with `size[0]/2` and re-called `view._positionGroup()` — `group.x` went from `NaN` to `84.5` (exactly `location.x - rect.x` for a healthy slider).

## Root cause

`src/component/dataZoom/SliderZoomView.ts:394`

```ts
            const normalizationConstant = size[0] / (thisDataExtent[1] - thisDataExtent[0]);
```

`thisDataExtent = data.getDataExtent(info.thisDim)` (line 380). With one data point — or with several points sharing the same value on the zoomed dimension — the extent is `[v, v]`, so the divisor is `0` and the constant is `Infinity`. Then at `src/component/dataZoom/SliderZoomView.ts:410-412`:

```ts
                thisCoord = isTimeAxis
                    ? (+thisValue - thisDataExtent[0]) * normalizationConstant
                    : thisCoord + step;
```

on a **time** axis this is `0 * Infinity === NaN`. The NaN is pushed into `areaPoints`/`linePoints` (lines 435-436), which become the `points` of the `graphic.Polygon`/`graphic.Polyline` built in `createDataShadowGroup` (lines 455-468) and added to `_displayables.sliderGroup`. `_positionGroup()` then does, at `src/component/dataZoom/SliderZoomView.ts:296-298`:

```ts
        const rect = thisGroup.getBoundingRect([sliderGroup]);
        thisGroup.x = location.x - rect.x;
        thisGroup.y = location.y - rect.y;
```

`rect.x` (and `rect.y` when the slider is vertical/rotated) is `NaN`, so the whole slider group is positioned at `NaN` — i.e. it is *not* at `_location` and effectively vanishes / lands wherever the renderer clamps it. **That is the "wrong position".**

Secondary, non-NaN symptom on the same code path: for non-time axes with `data.count() === 1`, `step = thisShadowExtent[1] / Math.max(1, 0) = size[0]` and `thisCoord` starts at `-step` (line 396), so the lone point is drawn at x = 0, the far-left edge — while the main axis centres a lone point (measured `dataToCoord` = 187.5 out of an axis extent of `[0,375]` for both time and category single-point series).

## Ruled out (do not change these)

- `_resetLocation()` (`SliderZoomView.ts:221-269`) and its local `positionInfo` object (lines 234-248) are **correct** in all single-point cases — `_location` and `_size` measured identical to the multi-point control.
- `_getViewExtent()` (`SliderZoomView.ts:302-304`, returns `[0, this._size[0]]`) is correct; `_handleEnds` measured `[0, 375]` and `_range` `[0, 100]` in every single-point case.
- `src/component/dataZoom/helper.ts` needs **no** change (it only holds axis-dim name mapping, `findEffectedDataZooms`, `collectReferCoordSysModelInfo`).
- `AxisProxy.calculateDataWindow` (`src/component/dataZoom/AxisProxy.ts:137-235`) survives the degenerate `dataExtent = [v, v]` because `linearMap` already special-cases a zero-width domain at `src/util/number.ts:65-69`.

## Edit 1 — `src/component/dataZoom/SliderZoomView.ts`, replace lines 391-396

Current (exact, 12-space indent):

```ts
            const areaPoints = [[size[0], 0], [0, 0]];
            const linePoints: number[][] = [];
            const step = thisShadowExtent[1] / (Math.max(1, data.count() - 1));
            const normalizationConstant = size[0] / (thisDataExtent[1] - thisDataExtent[0]);
            const isTimeAxis = info.thisAxis.type === 'time';
            let thisCoord = -step;
```

Replacement:

```ts
            const areaPoints = [[size[0], 0], [0, 0]];
            const linePoints: number[][] = [];
            const dataCount = data.count();
            const isTimeAxis = info.thisAxis.type === 'time';
            const thisDataSpan = thisDataExtent[1] - thisDataExtent[0];
            // When the series has only one data point (or every point shares the same
            // value on the zoomed dimension), the data extent degenerates to a zero
            // span: `size[0] / 0` is `Infinity` and `(v - v) * Infinity` is `NaN`, which
            // poisons the data shadow polygon, hence the bounding rect read by
            // `_positionGroup`, hence the position of the whole slider. Besides, a lone
            // point advanced by `step` would be stuck at the left edge. Draw the
            // degenerated shadow in the middle instead, which is where the main axis
            // places a lone data point as well.
            const isDegenerated = dataCount <= 1 || (isTimeAxis && !(thisDataSpan > 0));
            const middleCoord = size[0] / 2;
            const step = isDegenerated ? 0 : thisShadowExtent[1] / (dataCount - 1);
            const normalizationConstant = isDegenerated ? 0 : size[0] / thisDataSpan;
            let thisCoord = isDegenerated ? middleCoord : -step;
```

Note the `isTimeAxis` declaration is *moved up* — delete the old line 395 so there is no duplicate `const`. `Math.max(1, …)` is no longer needed because `dataCount >= 2` in the non-degenerate branch. `!(thisDataSpan > 0)` (rather than `=== 0`) also covers a `NaN` span.

## Edit 2 — `src/component/dataZoom/SliderZoomView.ts`, replace lines 410-412

Current (exact, 16-space indent, inside the `data.each(...)` callback):

```ts
                thisCoord = isTimeAxis
                    ? (+thisValue - thisDataExtent[0]) * normalizationConstant
                    : thisCoord + step;
```

Replacement:

```ts
                thisCoord = isDegenerated
                    ? middleCoord
                    : isTimeAxis
                    ? (+thisValue - thisDataExtent[0]) * normalizationConstant
                    : thisCoord + step;
```

(The nested-ternary formatting matches the existing style in `_positionGroup`, `SliderZoomView.ts:284-293`.)

The early-return stride branch at lines 403-408 needs no change: with `isDegenerated` the `step` is 0, and `stride = Math.round(data.count() / size[0])` (line 399) is 0 for a 1-point series so the branch is never taken.

## Edit 3 (recommended hardening) — `src/component/dataZoom/SliderZoomView.ts`, lines 295-298

Current (exact, 8-space indent):

```ts
        // Position barGroup
        const rect = thisGroup.getBoundingRect([sliderGroup]);
        thisGroup.x = location.x - rect.x;
        thisGroup.y = location.y - rect.y;
```

Replacement:

```ts
        // Position barGroup
        const rect = thisGroup.getBoundingRect([sliderGroup]);
        // Never let a degenerated (NaN) bounding rect leak into the group transform,
        // otherwise the whole slider is placed at NaN and disappears.
        thisGroup.x = location.x - (isFinite(rect.x) ? rect.x : 0);
        thisGroup.y = location.y - (isFinite(rect.y) ? rect.y : 0);
```

Bare `isFinite` is already used in this codebase (`src/chart/bar/BarView.ts:917`, `src/util/graphic.ts:856`), no import needed.

## Expected result after the fix

`xAxis:{type:'time'}` + 1 datum: `_shadowPolygonPts` becomes `[[375,0],[0,0],[187.5,15]]` and `group.x/group.y` become finite (`84.5 / 385.5` post-`_updateView`, matching the healthy multi-point slider). Vertical slider likewise gets a finite x and y.

